Proof connection
  The mod-13 certificate proves every AP boundary core directly.
  The sheet quotient is the reusable part: for bE plus h coprime parked
  runners, the same union bound gives a first floor
      meas(G_E) * (1 - h/7 - h/b),
  before any slow-fast V->infinity argument.  This is a finite-V bridge
  for non-AP coordinated-growth clusters with bounded h.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: sheet quotient > mod-13 residue > comb floor > raw V/b growth > runner vertices
  pairwise observable: certified positive lonely measure for S(b,V)
  challenged assumption: the hard core needs V/b large; sheet counting closes small V/b.
